🔄 Data Pipeline Design
This project is designed as a modular data pipeline, simulating how enterprise ETL systems operate.

🧩 Pipeline Stages
1️⃣ Data Extraction (Source Layer)
Data is sourced from curated domain-specific views:
sales.*
production.*
Purchasing.*
HumanResources.*
Person.*
Views act as a controlled abstraction layer over raw data

2️⃣ Staging Layer (Input Tables)
Data is loaded into Input_* tables
Purpose:
Isolate source changes
Enable reprocessing
Provide checkpointing

3️⃣ Transformation & Load (Output Tables)
Business logic applied inside child stored procedures
Data is written into Output_* tables
Current strategy:
Delete + Insert (idempotent load pattern)

4️⃣ Orchestration Layer
A Main Stored Procedure controls execution flow:
Executes child SPs sequentially
Maintains execution order using sequence_no
Handles success/failure tracking

5️⃣ Monitoring & Logging Layer
Ensures full pipeline observability

Session Level (Session_Log)

Tracks full pipeline run

Execution Level (Execution_Log)

Tracks each step:
Start time
End time
Rows processed
Status
Errors

🔁 Pipeline Characteristics

✔️ Modular – Each dataset is independently processed
✔️ Scalable – Easy to add new domains or SPs
✔️ Traceable – Full audit trail available
✔️ Restartable – Can rerun failed steps without affecting others
✔️ Deterministic – Same input produces same output

⚙️ Pipeline Execution Flow
Start Session
   ↓
Execute Child SP (Step 1)
   ↓
Log Execution
   ↓
Execute Child SP (Step N)
   ↓
End Session
🚀 Future Pipeline Enhancements
Add parallel execution for independent SPs
Introduce incremental loads (CDC)
Integrate with orchestration tools (ADF / Airflow)
Add data quality validation stage
Implement retry mechanism for failed steps

This pipeline design closely reflects real-world enterprise ETL systems, focusing on reliability, observability, and maintainability.
